        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 特点",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "特点 — tèdiǎn — \"characteristic; a distinguishing trait\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "这儿的菜有什么特点 zhèr de cài yǒu shénme tèdiǎn — What's special about the food here?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 特 (tè) — ten strokes in two pieces: on the left the cow piece, four strokes; on the right the earth piece of 地 over the right piece of 对. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "特点 (tèdiǎn) is built from 特 (tè) 'single, special' and 点 'a point', both inherited from Middle Chinese, dok and temX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first as a bull and 'alone' and the second as a dot made with the brush."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
